2. The selected elements are the first half of the modified list. Since the sum of these elements is `6`, we need to find a list of numbers that, after filtering and subtracting `10`, results in a list that can be split in half such that the sum of the first half is `6`.

3. The modified list is obtained by subtracting `10` from each even number greater than `10` in the input list. So, if the sum of the first half of the modified list is `6`, the original numbers that were greater than `10` and even must have been adjusted accordingly.

